  "question": {
    "text": "$\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\pi / 2} \\frac{\\left(1-\\tan \\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\right)(1-\\sin x)}{\\left(1+\\tan \\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\right)(\\pi-2 x)^{3}}=?$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$1 / 8$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "0",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1 / 32$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\infty$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Put $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}-h$ as $x \\rightarrow \\frac{\\pi}{2}, h \\rightarrow 0$\r\n$\\therefore$ Given limit\r\n$=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{1-\\tan \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2}\\right)}{1+\\tan \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2}\\right)} \\cdot \\frac{(1-\\cosh )}{(2 \\mathrm{~h})^{3}}$\r\n$=\\lim _{\\mathrm{h} \\rightarrow 0} \\tan \\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2} \\frac{2 \\sin ^{2} \\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2}}{8 \\mathrm{~h}^{3}}$\r\n$=\\lim _{\\mathrm{h} \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{\\tan \\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2}}{\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2} \\times 2}\\left(\\frac{\\sin \\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2}}{\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2}}\\right)^{2} \\times \\frac{1}{4}$\r\n$=\\lim _{\\mathrm{h} \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{1}{32} \\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\tan \\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2}}{\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2} \\times 2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\sin \\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2}}{\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2}}\\right)^{2}=\\frac{1}{32}$"
  }
}